00:56:33,920 --> 00:56:41,160
and focused in the face of life's difficulties. Self-care does not just mean resting or taking care of

486
00:56:41,160 --> 00:56:48,320
our body's basic needs; it goes much further. In the Stoic context,

487
00:56:48,320 --> 00:56:54,360
it's about cultivating strong mental health, maintaining a constant connection to our

488
00:56:54,360 --> 00:57:01,880
values ​​and purposes, and working to be the best version of ourselves. If we are not

489
00:57:01,880 --> 00:57:08,400
good with ourselves, if we do not nourish our body and our mind, we will never be able to offer

