698
01:21:21,280 --> 01:21:29,960
Finally, patience teaches us an important lesson: that the best things in life

699
01:21:29,960 --> 01:21:37,520
really do take time to materialize. The path to success, happiness, and

700
01:21:37,520 --> 01:21:44,520
inner peace is rarely quick or easy. But with patience, we can transform any

701
01:21:44,520 --> 01:21:52,000
adversity into an opportunity to grow. Patience prepares us for

702
01:21:52,000 --> 01:21:59,960
life's great challenges and gives us the wisdom necessary to face them with serenity and confidence.

703
01:21:59,960 --> 01:22:09,520
As Heraclitus stated: “Patience is bitter, but its fruit is sweet.” By embracing patience,

704
01:22:09,520 --> 01:22:15,800
we can reap the fruits of a fuller, more balanced, and, above all, wiser life.

